    "narrative": "As we push toward the final stretch of the season, **Corbin Carroll** headlines our daily outlook with an elite 70.82 score. Despite a sub-optimal seventh-order slotting, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Freeland, positioning him as our premier source for both power and the scarcity-driven stolen base potential we covet. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (67.47) and **Seiya Suzuki** (67.45) offer high-floor production; **Mickey Moniak** specifically leverages a 14% park advantage and a significant platoon edge against Soroka, while **Seiya Suzuki** maximizes his utility out of the #2 spot, providing the volume necessary to hunt category gains in R and RBI.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Isaac Paredes** (47.46) on the bench. While his dynamic platoon advantage against Gilbert is notable, he narrowly missed our efficiency floor due to the combination of a tough SP_xERA (3.42) and the uncertainty of a pending lineup. We opted to prioritize the higher raw output of **Josh Naylor** (67.40), whose matchup against Cristian Javier offers a stronger base projection and meaningful platoon leverage. Caution remains necessary regarding **Brice Turang** (48.11); while his elite sprint speed keeps him in the starting nine, he faces a stern test against Wheeler, further dampened by wind conditions and an elite catcher matchup that suppresses his overall efficiency score. Stay vigilant on the weather reports for the **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero** slots, as the \"wind in\" flags present a lingering risk to our power ceiling in those matchups.",
